<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The body colours of the insect castes: three per caste, and every mamono wears one.

		Which three belong to which caste is declared on the caste herself, in
		Defs/XenotypeDefs/Xenotypes_Insect.xml (a PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours modExtension),
		so a caste's palette reads where the caste is defined. A caste with no list - the four
		castes still to be built - keeps the shared chitin base tone on PMM_Gene_Insect instead.

		Why genes and not code: a gene's skinColorOverride is what vanilla paints her with
		(`Pawn_StoryTracker.SkinColor` reads `skinColorOverride ?? SkinColorBase`), it is saved
		with her, and it is what puts her one colour row on the gene page. Vanilla's own skin
		colours work this way too: the melanin genes are rolled per pawn, never listed.

		Why a roll and not a list: one skinColorOverride is one fixed RGB, so three colours need
		three defs - and listing all three on a xenotype leaves two greyed rows on her gene page
		(Pawn_GeneTracker.Notify_GenesChanged keeps one and overrides the rest). So no xenotype
		lists a colour: Source/Insects/InsectChitin.cs rolls one for her, and re-rolls every
		generated mamono - a daughter included, whose mother's colour arrives with her genes.

		The five shared tones this file held until 2026-09-30 are gone. A save made while they
		existed loses the gene reference once per pawn - the defs no longer exist, so the game
		logs it and drops it - and the roll above hands her a colour from her caste's palette on
		that same load, so she comes back in her caste's colours instead of staying untoned.

		Every colour parents off PMM_BaseSkinColour below, which carries what they share: the
		tone class (the marker the roll recognises a colour gene by), the Cosmetic_Skin category,
		the icon, the SkinColorOverride exclusion tag - so two can never stack - and
		randomBrightnessFactor pinned to 0, so the colour is exactly what the def says.
	-->

	<GeneDef Name="PMM_BaseSkinColour" ParentName="GeneSkinColorOverride" Abstract="True" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">
		<geneClass>PMM_Insects.Gene_InsectTone</geneClass>
		<displayOrderInCategory>1000</displayOrderInCategory>
		<randomBrightnessFactor>0</randomBrightnessFactor>
		<canGenerateInGeneSet>false</canGenerateInGeneSet>
	</GeneDef>

